{
  "name": "Locate811Ticket",
  "package": "beagle",
  "description": "Locate811Ticket — one Texas 811 locate ticket, from the prepared portal\n draft to the utilities' positive responses (D8; §1.6). Beagle's scripted\n routine (A20) writes it, never the model: PREPARED after the\n texas811.prepare_ticket pigeon saves a draft and the compare passes,\n PROPOSED once the submit_811_ticket proposal (A10) is filed, APPROVED on the\n company's thumb, FILED when the confirmation mail carries the ticket number,\n RESPONDED when texas811.read_ticket reports every utility in. A compare\n mismatch is PARKED with one crew.Report and never re-requested. No pigeon\n ever actuates Submit; a person submits the draft (PG2).\n JobPermits.locate_permit_id keeps pointing at the work.Permit once one\n exists. Updatable with the version guard (A4).\n RETENTION: OPERATIONAL (7 years after job close).",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "key",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 129 bytes",
        "minimum size: 1"
      ],
