        "description": "Blob is one promoted file: bytes that are fsynced and renamed into place on\n BOTH pods. A Blob row never points at bytes that are not on both pods (R9).\n\n IMMUTABLE AND CONTENT-ADDRESSED, PER TENANT (R5). Identity is\n `(group, namespace, content_hash)` and dedup is within a tenant and group\n only: two tenants holding the same bytes hold two files and each pays. A\n global key would have been a cross-tenant content oracle — ask whether a hash\n exists and learn that someone else has the document — and it contradicted\n DocHashIndex's own per-namespace rule.\n\n NO VERSIONING. A new version is a new blob and the consumer moves its own\n pointer. The filename is the consumer's and lives on BlobLink, not here.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "blob_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "blob_id is the record key and the file's path: `\u003cgroup\u003e/\u003cns\u003e/\u003csha256-hex\u003e`.\n Carried as one string rather than derived on read because it IS the key,\n and a key a reader has to assemble from three fields is a key two callers\n can assemble differently.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 512 bytes",
              "minimum size: 1"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 512,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_min_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "record_key": true
          },
          {
            "name": "group",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "group is the volume group this blob belongs to — the group whose rules\n admitted it. EQ-filterable because per-group quota accounting is a query\n over exactly this field plus `namespace`.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 64 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "content_hash",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "content_hash is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the bytes, computed by this\n service AS THE UPLOAD STREAMS — native and exact. It is checked against the\n client's declared hash at end of stream and the upload fails if they\n differ (R9 step 3).",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 64 bytes",
              "minimum size: 64"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_min_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "size_bytes",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "size_bytes is the byte count as counted on the wire, not as declared.",
            "constraints": [
              "must be \u003e= 0"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_ge",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 0,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "content_type",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "content_type is what `GET /b/` serves. It survived both the group's\n allow-list and the magic-byte sniff, so it describes the stored bytes\n rather than merely what the uploader said about them.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 128 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 128,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "created_ms",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "created_ms is when the blob was promoted. RANGE-filterable: \"what landed\n this week\" is a question about this field, and it is what a later GC over\n consumers' pointers (R12) would scan.",
            "constraints": [
              "must be \u003e= 0"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_ge",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 0,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "range"
          },
          {
            "name": "owner_principal",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "owner_principal is the OWNING SERVICE identity — docmanager, not blobstore\n — and the row's owning principal (R6). Only this identity creates or\n revokes links or deletes the blob.\n\n `spiffe_id` below is the record's declared owner but is the PUBLISHER,\n which is always blobstore, so it is the wrong field to filter an owner's\n reads on — the same split mailbox.MailboxEntry makes between `recipient`\n and `spiffe_id`.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq",
            "store_principal": true
          },
          {
            "name": "deleted",
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "deleted marks the blob logically gone. The BYTES are not deleted by the\n record: the owner's Delete is what unlinks them from both pods, and this\n flag is what stops a resolve and starts the purge clock."
          },
          {
            "name": "spiffe_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "spiffe_id is the record's owner in the store's sense — the publisher, which\n is blobstore's own workload identity. See owner_principal.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "namespace",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "namespace is the OWNING TENANT (R6) and the second segment of blob_id. It\n is what makes dedup per-tenant: the same bytes under two namespaces are two\n rows and two files.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq",
            "store_namespace": true
          },
          {
            "name": "trace_id",
            "type": "string",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "noop",
            "type": "bool"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "BlobLink",
  "package": "blobstore",
  "description": "BlobLink is one shareable URL, keyed by the HASH of its token (R7).\n\n THE RAW TOKEN APPEARS NOWHERE PERSISTENT. It is returned once, by the call\n that minted it, and this row holds only `sha256(token)`; ListLinks returns no\n tokens, and the gateway redacts `/b/*` and `/upload/*` paths from its logs.\n So a reader of the record store — or of a log, or of a backup — cannot\n resolve any link.\n\n REVOCATION IS IMMEDIATE, which is v3's improvement over the v2 signed-URL\n design: we serve the bytes, so `revoked_ms` is checked on every resolve\n rather than waiting for a cloud URL to expire. It is kept rather than deleted\n so an audit can still say a link existed.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "token_hash",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "token_hash is the record key: the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the raw token.\n A resolve hashes what arrived in the path and looks up THAT, so the lookup\n key is not a secret even though the path is.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 64 bytes",
        "minimum size: 64"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 64,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_min_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 64,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "record_key": true
    },
    {
      "name": "blob_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "blob_id is the Blob this link resolves to.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 512 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 512,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq"
    },
    {
      "name": "filename",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "filename is what `Content-Disposition` offers, and the ONLY source of it\n (R8) — never a client-supplied header, never a query parameter. Validated\n at mint: a basename, no CR/LF, quote, backslash, semicolon, control\n character or path separator.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 255 bytes",
        "minimum size: 1"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 255,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_min_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "policy",
      "type": "enum",
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_enum_defined",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "enum_values": [
        {
          "name": "LINK_POLICY_BEARER",
          "number": 1,
          "description": "BEARER: whoever holds the token. The only policy today (R7); SAME_TENANT\n and FLEET_ONLY are additive later and need a caller identity on the `/b/`\n path, which BEARER deliberately does not have."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "created_ms",
      "type": "int64",
      "constraints": [
        "must be \u003e= 0"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_ge",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 0,
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "expires_ms",
      "type": "int64",
      "description": "expires_ms is 0 for a durable shared link and non-zero for the short-lived\n one the owner mints for its own use. Checked on resolve alongside\n revoked_ms; the two are indistinguishable to the caller, who gets a 404\n either way.",
      "constraints": [
        "must be \u003e= 0"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_ge",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 0,
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "range"
    },
    {
