            "name": "blob_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "blob_id is the platform blob store's id for this document's bytes,\n `documents/\u003cnamespace\u003e/\u003ccontent_hash\u003e` — the same value DocHashIndex.blob_id\n carries for this row's content_hash. It is what makes a document a CONSUMER\n POINTER at a blob rather than a thing that owns bytes (blob store v3 R5: \"a\n consumer's record points at a hash and moves its own pointer\"), and it is\n the one field CreateDocFileLink below needs in order to call\n blobstore.CreateLink.\n\n It comes STRAIGHT FROM blobstore's CreateUploadResponse.blob_id, copied onto\n this row by the same CreateIngest handler that writes the DocHashIndex row\n from the same response (services/docmanager/src/service.rs, write_ingest) —\n NOT read back off the DocHashIndex row at this content_hash. That\n distinction is not a style choice: DocHashIndex has no `s2s_read` grant, so\n tacplus generates no reader over it, and a file_id -\u003e blob_id join through\n it is therefore not expressible today. Copying the value at ingest is the\n only path that exists, and it is safe to copy because a blob_id is derived\n entirely from (group, namespace, content_hash) and blobs are immutable, so\n the two copies cannot drift.\n\n DocHashIndex stays the per-tenant content_hash -\u003e blob_id index for dedup\n lookups; this field is the per-document pointer. Same 1024 bound\n DocHashIndex.blob_id uses, for the same value.\n See decisions/documents-volume-group-2026-09-26.md.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "trace_id",
            "type": "string",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "noop",
            "type": "bool"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "DocHashIndex",
  "package": "docmanager",
  "description": "DocHashIndex is the content-addressing index: a hash resolves to where the\n actual bytes live in the external object store. Near-infrastructure — this\n is NOT the customer-facing view of a document, which is DocFileMetadata\n below. One row per distinct content hash: identical bytes uploaded twice\n produce one row, which is the dedup the design doc calls out.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "content_hash",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "content_hash is the record key: the content hash of the file bytes\n (algorithm TBD — SHA-256 is the working assumption, not yet settled;\n flagging rather than silently picking one for the real pipeline).",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 128 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 128,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "record_key": true
    },
    {
      "name": "namespace",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "store_namespace: MANDATORY per the namespace-isolation decision. A hash\n index row is still per-tenant — two tenants uploading byte-identical\n files must not collide across the isolation boundary, even though the\n content hash alone would be identical. Dedup therefore happens WITHIN a\n namespace, not globally across tenants.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "store_namespace": true
    },
    {
      "name": "blob_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "blob_id is the platform blob store's id for these bytes:\n `documents/\u003cnamespace\u003e/\u003ccontent_hash\u003e`, the `documents` volume group\n declared on the service below. It is NOT assembled here — blobstore\n returns it from CreateUpload (blobstore.proto's CreateUploadResponse.blob_id,\n known before a byte moves because the key IS the declared content hash),\n and DocManager stores what it was given.\n\n This field was `object_store_location`, an opaque caller-supplied\n placeholder, until 2026-09-26. Same field number: the placeholder was\n renamed to the real value it always stood for, which is why the record\n shape did not have to change when the store was wired in.\n See decisions/documents-volume-group-2026-09-26.md.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1024,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "size_bytes",
      "type": "int64"
    },
    {
      "name": "indexed_at_ms",
      "type": "int64",
      "description": "indexed_at_ms is when this hash was first indexed. It was the retention\n clock until retention was removed (see the record option above); nothing\n measures from it today."
    },
    {
      "name": "ref_count",
      "type": "int64",
      "description": "ref_count is a hint for reclamation (delete the object once no\n DocFileMetadata row references this hash any more), maintained by\n DocManager's own write path, not derived by generation."
    },
    {
      "name": "owning_service",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "owning_service names DocManager's own service identity, NOT a customer.\n A hash-index row has no single natural owner — dedup means several\n customers' DocFileMetadata rows can reference the same content_hash\n within a namespace — so there is no per-user principal to declare\n honestly here. This record type still needs SOME (spec.store_principal)\n field: stratum hosts a generic RecordQuery/RecordMap c2s surface over\n EVERY (spec.record) in the fleet regardless of that record's own\n s2s/c2s declaration (confirmed by reading tacplus's\n recordprincipal_gen.go — javaRecordPrincipalUnenforceable fails\n generation for any (spec.record) with no resolvable owner, fleet-wide,\n not just for records that opt into the query trait themselves), so this\n field exists purely to satisfy that platform-wide constraint. Declaring\n the SERVICE as owner (same pattern spec.proto documents for\n service-emitted accounting rows) is also the semantically-honest answer\n AND fails closed: no human caller's token subject will ever equal a\n service identity, so DocHashIndex's (otherwise unused — see\n decisions/docmanageragent-read-path-open-2026-09-01.md, Reveille\n reads DocFileMetadata directly via its own stratum grant, not this\n trait) c2s query surface can never actually return rows to anyone.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 64 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 64,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "store_principal": true
    },
    {
      "name": "trace_id",
      "type": "string",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "noop",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ]
}

