                  "description": "retrieved_grace_seconds is INERT as of 2026-09-20 and is read by nothing.\n\n It had exactly one job: to defer the moment the sweep flipped a retrieved\n row's `ejectionable` from NEVER to WINDOW, so that a client which acks and\n then immediately re-reads still found the row resident. Both ends of that\n sentence are gone. The marker went with `spec.Ejectionable`, and residency\n is now a per-TYPE idle clock on the row's last touch — a grace period\n cannot shift it, because the retrieval write IS the touch.\n\n DECLARED, not deleted, on purpose: kernel holds mailbox's config, and\n removing the field is a config-compatibility question this migration has no\n answer for. It should be deleted and field 2 reserved in a follow-up once\n nothing in kernel sets it — see\n looper/schematic/workers/mailbox-ejectionable-migration-questions.md. The\n same now applies to sweep_interval_seconds above.",
