            "description": "revoked_at_ms is when the grant was revoked via Mint.RevokeGrant, epoch\n milliseconds. 0 means not revoked. A revoked grant is MARKED, never\n deleted, so the record remains as an audit trail of the delegation that\n existed and when it was withdrawn. Every mint from the grant and every\n later exchange of a token minted from it is denied once this is set\n (IdentityServiceImpl.assertGrantStillActive), so revocation kills\n already-minted derived tokens within one request.",
