{
  "name": "Delegate",
  "package": "kernel",
  "description": "Delegate holds bootstrap matchers for a service or machine client that can request tokens.\n Each delegate carries a name, which becomes the service path segment in the\n issued token's SPIFFE URI, and the namespace that URI is rooted at:\n spiffe://\u003ctrust-domain\u003e/system/\u003clocation\u003e/services/\u003cdelegate_name\u003e for a\n shared platform service, spiffe://\u003ctrust-domain\u003e/tenants/\u003ctenant\u003e/services/\u003cdelegate_name\u003e\n for a tenant-owned instance (see tenant_namespace).\n Authenticates via a projected Kubernetes service-account token or cloud identity.\n\n Two authorization models:\n   - S2S (identity-only): tokens carry only the SPIFFE URI as sub.\n     Receiving services enforce access via auth_services RE2 patterns\n     that match against the caller's service path.\n   - C2S (entitlement-based): OPA returns TokenEntitlements directly.\n     Kernel embeds expanded per-service RPC lists in the user token.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "name",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "name is the delegate's service path — becomes the final service path segment\n in the SPIFFE URI. For workload children: parent/\u003cchild\u003e.\n\n NOT unique on its own: a tenant-owned service has one delegate per tenant,\n all carrying the same name (the service path that auth_services patterns\n match on), distinguished only by tenant_namespace. The delegate's key is\n the (name, tenant_namespace) pair.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "tenant_namespace",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "tenant_namespace is the authorization namespace this delegate's minted\n identity is rooted at. Empty — the default, and what every shared platform\n service uses — means the /system root, so the minted subject is\n spiffe://\u003ctd\u003e/system/services/\u003cname\u003e. A tenant-owned service instance sets\n the canonical tenant namespace /tenants/\u003ctenant\u003e, and the minted subject\n becomes spiffe://\u003ctd\u003e/tenants/\u003ctenant\u003e/services/\u003cname\u003e, from which every\n token minted for it takes its namespace claim.\n\n This is the ONLY place a service's tenant is configured. Nothing a service\n sends can influence it: the tenant reaches the rest of the fleet solely as\n part of the SPIFFE subject kernel stamps here.\n\n Distinct from KubernetesServiceAccountMatcher.kubernetes_namespace, which\n is the K8s namespace the pod runs in, not an authorization namespace.",
