  "package": "kernel",
  "description": "TenantUserLink is one edge out of a linked tenant user: which identity in\n another tenant is the same human. Linking is GENERIC — any two tenants, not\n `people` and one other. The first use is drpepper's `jody` linked to that\n human's `people` row, but a contractor in two companies and a tenant\n migrating IdPs are the same record.\n\n peer_namespace, not a peer user path, is what the token's `linked` claim\n carries. The generated namespace backstop compares that claim against\n (spec.store_namespace), which holds a NAMESPACE, so a user path would never\n compare equal and a linked caller's read would never be accepted.",
  "fields": [
