      "name": "api_key",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "api_key is the secret, stored as given.\n\n NOT (spec.redact), and that is the point of this message existing rather than\n an omission: DROP would clear the field on the record plane's own read and\n leave this service unable to read back the key it wrote (file header). What\n keeps it safe is that no response message anywhere carries this type.\n\n Not a (spec.query_field) either, on top of the general rule that a filterable\n secret is a guessing oracle: nothing queries by key value, and the point read\n on `owner` is the only access this row has.",
