              "description": "BusinessHours is when this person is taken to be working. It is KNOWLEDGE in\n §1's sense — \"what was learned\" — not a setting, and nothing in the API lets\n a caller author it.\n\n TWO LAYERS, and `source` says which one produced the values in this message:\n\n   PRIOR    — an industry+geography default, which is what a brand-new record\n              with zero history has. It is a guess, and it is marked as one.\n   OBSERVED — refined from the person's own recorded activity once there is\n              enough of it to say anything.\n\n Only the PRIOR layer is WRITTEN today. The observed layer is shape here and\n nothing else, deliberately: the naive refinement (widen the window to cover\n every hour a read was seen at) would defeat the thing the deferral exists to\n protect — one 11pm read would make 11pm business hours. That is a question\n about what evidence of \"working\" means, not an implementation detail, and it\n is written up rather than guessed. See\n loopers/schematic/decisions/business-hours-inferred-not-configured.md.\n\n SINGLE CONCEPT. This is the same \"business hours\" feature-ideas.md's loop\n cadence needs (\"looped more frequently Mon-Fri during business hours\"). Do\n not add a second notion of it.",
