  "description": "GetMyTicketAuditResponse deliberately has NO advice field, exactly as\n GetTicketResponse does not.\n\n §3's \"Joe sees the decision and Dennis's comment. Not the advice\" is a rule\n about the REQUESTER, and this response is scoped to tickets the caller\n requested — so returning advice here would hand every requester the advice\n their decider was given, through a new transport, after the gRPC surface\n spent a whole separate RPC keeping it from them. A second surface that\n quietly relaxes the first one's rule is the drift the typed-contract argument\n exists to prevent.",
