      "description": "artifacts are the ScottyActivity rows for the tickets above, read out of\n the RECORD STORE rather than out of kernel state — the only field here\n that does not come from ScottyState.\n\n Why it belongs on this rpc and nowhere else: §1's \"nothing reaches\n knowledge without leaving an artifact\" is a claim about what is on the\n record, and until now the only way a PERSON could read those rows was the\n shared `query` trait's c2s half, where any token holding aud=query reads\n every record type in the fleet. decisions/mcp-generation-and-service-owned-\n data-2026-08-31.md §1 calls that superseded and §4 says the read belongs on\n the owning service's own surface. This is that surface, and its arrival is\n what lets vservices/query.proto be deleted (BIG GOAL 8 phase 2 item 10).\n\n SCOPE IS UNCHANGED, and that is the whole reason this could be added\n without settling the org-hierarchy question: the rows returned are those of\n the tickets `tickets` already carries, which are the tickets the caller\n REQUESTED. Not \"artifacts I wrote\" (that would reach my comments on other\n people's tickets) and not \"artifacts about me\" (that would need the\n hierarchy). Same predicate as the three fields above, one more field —\n see decisions/item10-c2s-replacement-2026-09-01.md.\n\n ADVICE IS NOT LEAKED BY THIS. A ScottyActivity row carries what was DONE —\n entity kind, entity id, principal, request id — and never what was said, so\n the artifact of a CreateTicketAdvice discloses that advice was sealed, not\n its text. The response's no-advice rule above is about advice CONTENT and\n is untouched. Only SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_TICKET rows are returned in any case.\n\n Bounded at 200 like the two append-only sides. The handler stops reading\n once it has that many rather than reading every ticket and truncating,\n because each ticket's rows cost a query against the store.",
