{
  "name": "ChatMembership",
  "package": "scottypersonal",
  "description": "ChatMembership is what ONE person has decided about one chat: archived,\n muted, what they told their Scotty to do about it, how far they have read.\n None of it is anyone else's business and none of it is shared, which is why\n this row can carry the pin `Chat` cannot.\n\n It is also the chat list. Every read of \"my chats\" goes through here, so the\n generated per-principal filter is the list's authorization, not a check.\n\n A stratum record since 2026-09-25, principal-owned and NOT `private` — read\n the (spec.record_read) block at the top of this file for why `private` is the\n right description of this row and the wrong annotation for it today.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "membership_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "membership_id is the record key: \"\u003cchat_id\u003e/\u003cprincipal\u003e\". Derived rather\n than minted, exactly as ChatSession.session_id is and for the same reason:\n one row per (chat, person) by construction.\n\n (spec.indexed) is gone with the state collection — see Chat.chat_id.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 900 bytes",
