{
  "name": "ChatSession",
  "package": "scottypersonal",
  "description": "ChatSession is what one person's Scotty is currently holding in mind about\n one chat. It is knowledge, re-derivable from ChatEvent; it is not an\n artifact, which is why this service's state root carries no\n requires_artifact_on_write. What Scotty DOES from a chat leaves its artifact\n where the doing happens — a ticket in the tenant that owns it.\n\n A stratum record since 2026-09-25, principal-owned and NOT `private` — see\n the (spec.record_read) block at the top of this file. THIS is the one type in\n this file that `private` would fit on its own terms (it is never read across\n owners); it stays non-private with its siblings because the reader it would\n need does not exist, and because one private row among three ordinary ones\n buys a second plane client and no guarantee the store_principal pin does not\n already give.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "session_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "session_id is the record key: \"\u003cchat_id\u003e/\u003cprincipal\u003e\". Derived rather than\n minted, so one person has exactly one session per chat by construction and\n a second one cannot be created by racing.\n\n (spec.indexed) is gone with the state collection — see Chat.chat_id.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 900 bytes",
        "minimum size: 1"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 900,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_min_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "record_key": true
    },
    {
      "name": "chat_id",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 600 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 600,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "principal",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "principal is the OWNING principal, and it is the whole egress mechanism for\n this collection: (spec.store_principal) generates the read-side filter that\n pins every surface returning this row to the caller's own subject.\n\n It is the PERSONAL principal (login doc §2b: the device's synced keychain\n key), never a per-tenant identity. That is the split: this row is one\n person's, across every tenant they belong to, and there is no tenant-scoped\n reader of it at all.\n\n EQ-queryable since 2026-09-25 — see ChatMembership.principal for why that\n is half the annotation and not decoration.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq",
      "store_principal": true
    },
    {
      "name": "state_text",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "state_text is the ONE generic text field Jody asked for: the LLM gets it,\n modifies it, puts it back whole. Nothing parses it, nothing derives\n authority from it, and NO FACT MAY LIVE ONLY HERE — see the 2026-09-07\n decision doc §2. In particular the routing map is not remembered here: it\n is read from kernel every time (login doc §4, and GetMyRoutingMap below).",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 65536 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 65536,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "state_version",
      "type": "int64",
      "description": "state_version increments on every replace and must be presented on the\n next replace. A stale replace is FAILED_PRECONDITION. Cheap insurance\n against a dormant session that woke twice."
    },
    {
      "name": "last_active_at_ms",
      "type": "int64"
    },
    {
      "name": "namespace",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "namespace is the row's owning namespace, held to the reader's claim by\n exact equality by the generated egress filter.\n\n WHAT VALUE A PERSONAL PRINCIPAL'S ROWS CARRY IS NOT SETTLED, and this is\n the one place the service split reaches down to a field. Device principals\n do not exist yet (login doc §6 item 1) and nothing has decided what\n namespace claim one holds. What IS settled is that it must not be a\n TENANT's: a personal chat spans every tenant the person belongs to, so\n pinning the row to one tenant would contradict §3's \"the personal runtime\n sees everything the user sees\".\n\n The field is kept — with the marker — rather than dropped, because\n (spec.store_namespace) is only mandatory on a (spec.record) and a state row\n may legally omit it, which would mean silently generating NO egress\n backstop at all. Whoever settles the device-principal claim settles this\n field's value; the annotation is not the thing to remove if it turns out\n the claim is empty.\n\n MANDATORY NOW, not merely kept: tacplus's ValidateRecordNamespaceAnnotations\n fails generation for a (spec.record) declaring no such field, \"on the\n reasoning that the record nobody remembered to annotate is exactly the one\n that leaks\". The paragraph above anticipated this (\"(spec.store_namespace)\n is only mandatory on a (spec.record)\") — the move to stratum is what made\n it so. EQ-queryable because c2s_read requires it.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq",
      "store_namespace": true
    },
    {
      "name": "spiffe_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "spiffe_id is the record's declared `owner` and the PUBLISHER — this\n SERVICE, never the person. See Chat.spiffe_id.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1024,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "trace_id",
      "type": "string",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "noop",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ]
}

