            "description": "spiffe_id is the record's declared `owner` and the PUBLISHER — eventbus\n stamps weather's own service identity onto it. The field NAME is load-bearing\n (eventbus's topic discovery matches the literal string \"spiffe_id\" of string\n type when it decides which topics get publisher-identity stamping), which is\n why it carries (spec.identity_spiffe_subject).\n\n ON THIS SERVICE IT IS THE ONLY OWNERSHIP STATEMENT THERE IS, and it is the\n true one: these rows belong to the platform's weather service, which is\n exactly what a 9a service's rows are. It is never a read filter — every row\n of every one of these four types carries the same value.",
