{
  "name": "WeatherState",
  "package": "weather",
  "description": "WEATHERSTATE IS EMPTY, and that is the whole point of it — the same statement\n profile.ProfileState and (since 2026-09-25) work.WorkState make, in the same\n words, for the same reason.\n\n It exists because servicemanager's generated wiring requires every service in\n the build to host one state root, not because this service keeps anything in\n kernel. Jody's 2026-09-25 ruling is explicit — \"kernel is in-memory\n coordination only\" — so a field added here later is a CHANGE OF STORAGE PLANE,\n not a new field.\n\n WHAT WAS HERE, and where it went. Four `repeated` collections — places,\n observations, forecasts, alerts — each carrying (spec.persistence) = true,\n which the ruling's item 2 turns into a generation error (\"durable data belongs\n in stratum records\"). Every one is now a (spec.record) below. The dev rows that\n were in kernel are lost on the next full kernel restart and that is accepted\n (ruling item 5); for this service in particular that costs less than for any\n other, because every row is re-fetchable from api.weather.gov EXCEPT the\n history, and the Places are re-registered by their callers.\n\n THE COLLECTION BOUNDS WENT WITH THE FIELDS, and one of them was load-bearing:\n max_places in Config is the bound that survives, checked in the CreatePlace\n handler. assert_max_size 10000000 on observations was never enforcement, it was\n a statement of scale, and the scale is why three of the four records below\n declare (spec.query_field) pushdowns where `work` declared none.\n\n No requires_artifact_on_write, unlike work.WorkState and scotty.ScottyState.\n See the (spec.record_read) note above — choice C. Note that `work` REMOVED its\n option in the same migration and `scotty` KEPT its; neither applies here,\n because this file never declared one.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "trace_id",
      "type": "string",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "noop",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ]
}

