            "type": "string",
            "description": "assigned_to is the principal the task is FOR.\n\n NO (spec.store_principal) HERE, and that is choice B's answer rather than\n its abandonment. A task is read by TWO people — the one it is for and the\n one who raised it — and tacplus pins to exactly one: principal_validate.go\n refuses a second (spec.store_principal)/(spec.principal) field on one\n message, and (spec.record_read).c2s.scope has no \"principal in one of these\n fields\" value. Pinning to assigned_to alone would make the person who\n RAISED the task unable to see it, which is the wrong half to keep.\n\n So the two-principal gate is where scotty.Ticket already puts the identical\n problem: in the handler. scotty's `is_participant` admits the requester who\n opened a ticket or the decider it is routed to; work's task reads admit\n assigned_to or raised_by, by the same construction and for the same reason.\n Anything WIDER than those two — a superintendent's view of the crew's tasks\n — is the unbuilt entitlement work `scotty.Human` is already waiting on\n (schematic looper's decisions/scotty-read-authorization-not-wired.md,\n pre-split snoopy history, not in this repo) and is not invented here.",
