            "name": "store_epoch_ms",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "store_epoch_ms is this row's LAST-WRITE clock, Unix milliseconds, owned and\n stamped by the generated wrapper — a producer that supplies one is refused\n (INVALID_ARGUMENT), so the value can never be caller-influenced.\n\n It is what makes AgentEvent REPLAYABLE in stratum's hot tier: each node's\n redo log is partial, so recovery is a union across nodes and the epoch is\n the only clock that resolves it. Without this field the type keeps its\n in-memory replication and its quorum gate but gets no redo log at all\n (stratum's HotStoreGenerator refuses one it could not safely merge).\n\n NOT timestamp_ms: that is the author's business clock. Two different\n clocks; only this one is store-owned.",
            "filter_mode": "range"
