        "description": "Chat is who is in a conversation. It is the one row in this service that\n belongs to SEVERAL people at once, and that is the whole difficulty with it.\n\n NO (spec.store_principal), AND THAT IS NOT AN OMISSION. The annotation pins a\n row to exactly one subject — tacplus refuses a second field carrying it\n (`principal_validate.go`, recorded in decisions/work-service-2026-09-09.md\n VERIFY answer 4) — and a chat with four participants has no one owner to pin\n to. `created_by` would pin reads to the creator and hide the chat from\n everyone else in it. So this collection gets NO generated egress filter, and\n \"only a member may read a chat\" is a hand-written check in the handler,\n enforced against the caller's own ChatMembership row.\n\n That is the same unbuilt entitlement gap `scotty.Human` records (see\n schematic/looper/schematic/decisions/scotty-read-authorization-not-wired.md)\n and it is NOT solved here. What IS structural is the membership row: every\n list of chats goes through ChatMembership, which is principal-pinned, so the\n only way to learn a chat_id you are not in is to be told one.\n\n A stratum record since 2026-09-25, and the ONE of this file's four with no\n owning principal — which is exactly what decides its record shape. Read the\n (spec.record_read) block at the top of this file for why it gets no c2s half.",
