          {
            "name": "namespace",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "namespace is MANDATORY on a record and is `/system` ON EVERY ROW OF THIS\n TYPE — the namespace of this service's own identity, not any tenant's. Read\n the block above this message for the whole argument; the short form is that a\n Place has no owning tenant by construction, `/system` is what the platform's\n own rule reduces `/system/services/weather` to, and the field deliberately\n carries no (spec.query_field) so that no read pins a criterion that could not\n narrow anything and would cost the store's by-key fast path.\n\n A HAZARD THIS FIELD NOW CARRIES, AND IT IS A TACPLUS GAP RATHER THAN A DESIGN\n CHOICE. Making these types records turns on the generated WATCH egress\n backstop, which compares EVERY snapshot frame and EVERY delta against the\n CALLER'S namespace claim and calls std::process::abort() on a mismatch. The\n unary and PAGE seams apply that filter only for a c2s service or the record\n plane's own s2s wrapper, and they carry a `__ns_pinned` escape so a /system\n peer keeps a fleet-wide read; the WATCH seam\n (rust/types/servicewrapper_gen.go:1511-1517 against :1882/:1947) has NEITHER\n gate. So today:\n\n   - every caller on this service's auth_services list is a SHARED service\n     whose own namespace claim is `/system`, so `/system` on the row MATCHES\n     and the three WATCH rpcs work;\n   - the day a TENANT-OWNED service watches this one — which is exactly what\n     `reveille` is meant to be — its claim is `/tenants/\u003ct\u003e` , the guard\n     mismatches, AND WEATHER'S PROCESS ABORTS. Not a refused call: an abort.\n\n There is no value of this field that avoids that, because a fleet-shared row\n read by callers in different namespaces cannot equal all of their claims.\n The fix is in tacplus, not here: the WATCH seam needs the same gate its unary\n and PAGE siblings have. Recorded in\n decisions/weather-record-shapes-2026-09-25.md as the one thing that must land\n before `reveille` exists.",
