            "description": "owner_principal: who owns this file. (spec.store_principal), NOT\n (spec.principal) — the latter is for a REQUEST field the wrapper stamps\n from the caller's subject on the way IN; this is a RECORD field naming\n the row's owning principal for egress filtering (every c2s read of this\n record type is filtered down to rows the caller owns). Found the\n distinction by hitting stratum's real generation error: \"RecordQuery\n ...GetDocFileMetadataSample cannot be generated for a c2s surface\n because its response field 'items' carries (spec.record) rows declaring\n no owner the wrapper can filter on\" — (spec.principal) doesn't count as\n that, only (spec.store_principal) does. CreateIngestRequest.owner_principal\n below is a genuine request field, so it correctly keeps (spec.principal).",
