            "name": "spiffe_actor",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "spiffe_actor is the ORIGIN signal: the delegate that made the call, stamped\n by EventBus from the publishing token's `act` claim at publish time.\n\n   \"a message is marked as originating from the user directly or from the\n    user's Scotty acting on their behalf... A message sent by\n    Scotty-for-Dennis carries `act` populated; one Dennis sends directly\n    doesn't.\" — decisions/messaging-vs-ticketing-2026-08-31.md\n\n The service does not set it and must not: like spiffe_id above, a value\n written here would be a claim about identity that nothing verified.\n Provenance only — sys/spec.proto forbids wiring it into a principal.\n\n GAP, STATED NOT PAPERED OVER. That quote describes the pre-supersession\n model, where the user published to EventBus DIRECTLY and EventBus saw the\n user's own delegated token. Under the corrected model the publish is s2s\n from messaging, so the token EventBus stamps from is messaging's own\n service token and carries no `act` claim at all — this field will be empty\n in the ordinary case, including for a genuine Scotty-for-Dennis send. The\n annotation is declared anyway, and correctly: the seam is the right one and\n the field is where the value belongs the moment the delegated-publish path\n exists. Closing it needs an s2s publish that carries the caller's exchanged\n token, which the generated publisher does not offer today. Written up in\n workers/big8-p1-messaging-questions.md rather than hand-rolled around.",
