            "description": "position is a SORTABLE STRING KEY, fractional/lexicographic — not an int.\n The ruling: \"a drag-to-reorder is a single-row write with no renumbering of\n siblings.\" Siblings sort by byte order of this value; a node dropped\n between two neighbours gets a key that sorts between theirs.\n\n The generation scheme is the runtime's business and not fixed here, beyond\n the one property the ordering depends on: keys must compare correctly as\n BYTES, so no scheme may produce a key that is a prefix-extension of an\n adjacent one in a way that reorders. Ties are broken by node_id wherever\n this field is ordered on, so equal positions are survivable rather than\n silently non-deterministic.",
