        {
          "name": "RECORD_CHANGE_TYPE_DELETE",
          "number": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "item",
      "type": "message",
      "message": {
        "name": "WorkActivity",
        "package": "work",
        "description": "WorkActivity is the ARTIFACT left by every write into knowledge, and it is\n scotty.ScottyActivity's shape field for field — including the annotations,\n which is the part a copy-by-shape gets wrong. See scotty.proto for the long\n form of each; the short form is:\n\n   - acted_by carries (spec.store_principal) + an EQ (spec.query_field): it is\n     the authenticated human the write happened FOR, and it is the field the\n     c2s record-read plane filters a person's own rows by.\n   - spiffe_id is the record's declared `owner` and is the PUBLISHER —\n     eventbus stamps work's own service identity onto it. The field NAME is\n     load-bearing (eventbus's topic discovery matches the literal string\n     \"spiffe_id\" of string type when it decides which topics get\n     publisher-identity stamping), and it carries\n     (spec.identity_spiffe_subject) for the same reason ScottyActivity's does.\n     Filtering a person's reads on THIS field would show them every row in the\n     tenant while looking like it showed them their own, which is why acted_by\n     above is the principal and this is not.\n   - namespace must be EQ-queryable or tacplus refuses (spec.record).c2s_read:\n     the client-facing read plane pins the field to the caller's verified\n     namespace claim before the store is asked, and a pin needs a criterion to\n     be pinned into.\n\n spec.record implies spec.event, so tacplus synthesizes the topic wrapper\n WorkActivityBus with topic ref work.WorkActivityBus.stream. Do NOT hand-write\n that wrapper.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "activity_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "activity_id is the record key: one row per WRITE, not one per entity.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 160 bytes",
