    {
      "name": "store_epoch_ms",
      "type": "int64",
      "description": "store_epoch_ms is this row's LAST-WRITE clock, Unix milliseconds, owned and\n stamped by the generated wrapper — a producer that supplies one is refused\n (INVALID_ARGUMENT), so the value can never be caller-influenced.\n\n It is what makes AgentEvent REPLAYABLE in stratum's hot tier: each node's\n redo log is partial, so recovery is a union across nodes and the epoch is\n the only clock that resolves it. Without this field the type keeps its\n in-memory replication and its quorum gate but gets no redo log at all\n (stratum's HotStoreGenerator refuses one it could not safely merge).\n\n NOT timestamp_ms: that is the author's business clock. Two different\n clocks; only this one is store-owned.",
      "filter_mode": "range"
    },
    {
      "name": "namespace",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "namespace is the row's owning TENANT — the namespace claim of the principal\n whose session produced this event. It is the tenant half of the identity\n spiffe_id carries the subject half of: spiffe_id names WHO acted, this names\n WHICH TENANT the row belongs to, and the generated egress filter holds a c2s\n read to rows matching the caller's claim by EXACT equality (never the\n level-or-below containment the administrative namespace rule uses).\n\n MANDATORY, not opt-in: tacplus (ValidateRecordNamespaceAnnotations) fails\n generation for any (spec.record) declaring no such field, on the reasoning\n that the record nobody remembered to annotate is exactly the one that leaks.\n\n The filter is generated on the READ side, which is not this record's own\n s2s publish surface above: stratum's record query plane (the (spec.trait) in\n the app proto's vservices/query.proto) exposes a c2s List/Sample/Watch over\n EVERY record in the fleet, and the namespace check is spliced into each of\n them for this type. A row reaching one of those with a namespace other than\n the caller's halts the JVM rather than failing the one call.\n\n Deliberately NOT projected into any transformation above: adding it there\n would widen four already-explicit column lists, which is a separate call.",
