            ],
            "enum_values": [
              {
                "name": "CHAT_KIND_SELF_CHAT",
                "number": 1,
                "description": "SELF: the user and their own Scotty. Goes nowhere. Many per user.\n\n NAMED _SELF_CHAT AND NOT _SELF, and that is a tacplus defect worked around\n rather than a shade of meaning. `CHAT_KIND_SELF` renders as the Rust variant\n `Self`, which is a reserved word: prost's own emitter sanitizes it to\n `Self_`, but tacplus's `toProstEnumVariant`\n (pkg/internal/rust/types/enums.go:229) PascalCases without consulting its\n own `rustKeywords` set, so the serde and helper files it generates alongside\n say `ChatKind::Self` and the model crate does not compile:\n   error[E0433]: `Self` in paths can only be used in start position\n     types/services/scottypersonal/helpers.rs:25  \"chat-kind-self\" =\u003e Ok(ChatKind::Self)\n     types/services/scottypersonal/scottypersonal.serde.rs:2364  Self::Self =\u003e \"CHAT_KIND_SELF\"\n (verified 2026-09-11 against tacplus c33d7d56 by building services/work,\n the first Rust service generated since this enum landed). The upstream fix\n is for toProstEnumVariant to mirror prost's trailing-underscore rule; until\n it does, no proto in this fleet may end an enum value in _SELF. Rename this\n back the day that lands — nothing has ever been stored under either name."
              },
              {
                "name": "CHAT_KIND_DIRECT",
                "number": 2,
                "description": "DIRECT: two people (and their Scottys). One per pair."
              },
              {
                "name": "CHAT_KIND_GROUP",
                "number": 3,
                "description": "GROUP: people who join and leave."
              },
              {
                "name": "CHAT_KIND_JOB",
                "number": 4,
                "description": "JOB: a GROUP whose closure is company-wide. Reserved from the 2026-09-07\n sketch: the job type does not exist yet and nothing here invents it."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "participants",
            "type": "message",
            "description": "participants are HUMAN principals and AGENT identities. The caller's own\n Scotty is implicit in every chat and is not listed; a participant of kind\n AGENT is a NAMED one (a DocManager, a JobManager, a customer's agent).\n\n A PARTICIPANT IS A PERSONAL PRINCIPAL, not a per-tenant identity, for the\n same reason ChatSession.principal is: the chat spans every tenant its\n members belong to. A member of this chat is not thereby a member of any\n tenant — where work gets FILED is the routing map's business, and\n GetMyRoutingMap answers it separately for each person.",
