          "name": "RECORD_CHANGE_TYPE_DELETE",
          "number": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "item",
      "type": "message",
      "message": {
        "name": "Message",
        "package": "messaging",
        "description": "Message is ONE DELIVERY: one message, to one recipient.\n\n It is NOT one row per submission. A submission naming three recipients\n becomes three `Message` rows sharing a `message_id`, differing in\n `delivery_id` and `recipient`, each independently consumable and\n independently ACKable. See the fan-out note at the top of this file for why\n EventBus cannot do that split itself.\n\n spec.record implies spec.event, so tacplus synthesizes the topic wrapper\n MessageBus with topic ref messaging.MessageBus.stream. Do NOT hand-write that\n wrapper.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "delivery_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "delivery_id is the record key: \"\u003cmessage_id\u003e/\u003crecipient\u003e\". One per\n (message, recipient) pair, which is what makes the N publishes of one\n submission N separately-keyed records rather than N copies of one.\n\n Derived rather than random ON PURPOSE: the value a caller would need to\n reconstruct to ACK a delivery is exactly (which message, for whom), so\n deriving it means an agent that knows both never has to have been told the\n id. It is also what makes the fan-out replay-safe — a retried submission\n regenerates the same delivery ids rather than a second set of rows.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 512 bytes",
              "minimum size: 1"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 512,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_min_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "record_key": true
          },
          {
            "name": "message_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "message_id groups the N deliveries of ONE submission. EQ-filterable,\n because \"every delivery of the message I sent\" is the question a sender\n asks, and it is the only way back from a delivery to its siblings.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 128 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 128,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "sender",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "sender is who sent it — the authenticated principal subject bound by the\n (spec.principal) field on SendMessageRequest below, never a caller-written\n string.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "recipient",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "recipient is THE recipient this delivery is for — one of `recipients`\n below, and the half of delivery_id that varies across the fan-out.\n\n It is also the ROW'S OWNING PRINCIPAL for the record query plane's c2s\n half. spiffe_id below is the record's declared owner but is the PUBLISHER —\n eventbus stamps messaging's own service identity onto it — so filtering a\n user's reads on that field would show every user nothing. `sender` is the\n other candidate and is the wrong one: a mailbox read is \"messages addressed\n to me\", so the field the generated egress filter holds a caller's reads to\n must be the addressee.\n\n The consequence is stated rather than hidden: a SENDER cannot read their own\n sent messages through this record's c2s plane, because only one field may\n carry (spec.store_principal) and this is it. Sent-items is a mailbox\n concern and the mailbox service is Phase 1 item 8, undesigned; inventing a\n second read path for it here would be inventing that service's shape.\n\n The EQ criterion is what carries the row filter into the plane's SIZE-ONLY\n RPCs: Get\u003cT\u003eCount returns a number over the handle's predicate and no rows,\n so no egress filter can narrow it. The generated c2s wrapper pins this\n criterion to the caller at Create\u003cT\u003eQuery and every later call on the\n handle inherits it.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq",
            "store_principal": true
          },
          {
            "name": "recipients",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "recipients is the full To: line — every recipient of the submission, the\n SAME list on all N deliveries. `recipient` above says which one this row is\n for; this says who else got it.\n\n Carrying it is not redundancy. Without it a recipient cannot see who else\n was addressed, which is information the sender chose to disclose by\n addressing them together — the same reason a To: header exists and a Bcc:\n one does not. (This file models no Bcc; nothing has asked for one.)\n\n Bounded at 256 to match Config.max_recipients' ceiling above.",
            "repeated": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 elements",
              "maximum element size: 32768 bytes (default)"
