      "message": {
        "name": "BlobLinkStats",
        "package": "blobstore",
        "description": "BlobLinkStats is the coarse rollup of one link's resolutions (R10).\n\n The counters live IN MEMORY on the pod that served the request and are\n flushed here at most once a minute per token. That is the whole design: a\n `/b/` resolve must not cost a record write, and nobody needs a resolution\n count to be exact.\n\n `bytes_served` is honest here in a way it could not be in the v2 cloud\n design: we serve the bytes ourselves, so we count them rather than inferring\n them from a signed URL that may or may not have been followed.\n\n TWO PODS, TWO COUNTERS. Each pod flushes what it served, and a flush is a\n read-modify-write of this row — so the row is the SUM only as of the last\n flush either pod made. Exactness was never on offer for an in-memory counter;\n what matters is that a flush never loses another pod's contribution, which is\n why it reads before it adds.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "token_hash",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "token_hash is the key, and the same key BlobLink carries — the two rows are\n one link's two halves, split because the stats half is rewritten on a\n minute cadence and the link half is written once.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 64 bytes",
              "minimum size: 64"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
