      "message": {
        "name": "ChatEvent",
        "package": "scottypersonal",
        "description": "ChatEvent is the append-only record of what was said and what Scotty did. One\n row per OWNER copy, which is what makes history entitleable per person with\n no hand-written check: `owner` carries (spec.store_principal) and the\n generated filter does the rest.\n\n A stratum record since 2026-09-25, principal-owned and NOT `private` — see\n the (spec.record_read) block at the top of this file, whose second reason is\n about THIS type: one logical event is one row per member, and appending it\n reads every other member's high-water seq. A pin that admits only the\n caller's own rows cannot do that.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "event_key",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "event_key is the record key: \"\u003cevent_id\u003e/\u003cowner\u003e\". event_id for a sent\n message is \"\u003cchat_id\u003e/\u003csender\u003e/\u003cclient_message_id\u003e\", which is what makes a\n retried send rewrite the same rows instead of appending duplicates.\n Service-originated events mint event_id timestamp-first.\n\n (spec.indexed) is gone with the state collection — see Chat.chat_id.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1200 bytes",
              "minimum size: 1"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1200,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_min_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "record_key": true
