          {
            "name": "recipient",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "recipient is THE recipient this delivery is for — one of `recipients`\n below, and the half of delivery_id that varies across the fan-out.\n\n It is also the ROW'S OWNING PRINCIPAL for the record query plane's c2s\n half. spiffe_id below is the record's declared owner but is the PUBLISHER —\n eventbus stamps messaging's own service identity onto it — so filtering a\n user's reads on that field would show every user nothing. `sender` is the\n other candidate and is the wrong one: a mailbox read is \"messages addressed\n to me\", so the field the generated egress filter holds a caller's reads to\n must be the addressee.\n\n The consequence is stated rather than hidden: a SENDER cannot read their own\n sent messages through this record's c2s plane, because only one field may\n carry (spec.store_principal) and this is it. Sent-items is a mailbox\n concern and the mailbox service is Phase 1 item 8, undesigned; inventing a\n second read path for it here would be inventing that service's shape.\n\n The EQ criterion is what carries the row filter into the plane's SIZE-ONLY\n RPCs: Get\u003cT\u003eCount returns a number over the handle's predicate and no rows,\n so no egress filter can narrow it. The generated c2s wrapper pins this\n criterion to the caller at Create\u003cT\u003eQuery and every later call on the\n handle inherits it.",
