        "description": "PolicyVersion is ONE version of one written policy, and it is immutable.\n\n §2, and the word doing the work is \"written\": \"A written policy has a\n document, an author and a date, so policy is quotable or it isn't policy —\n which converts 'Scotty invented a company policy' from a prompt problem into\n a structural one.\"\n\n So all four properties are fields, not conventions: body (the document),\n authored_by_human_id (the author), authored_at_ms (the date) and\n effective_from_ms + version (the \"at the time\" axis). There is no\n UpdatePolicyVersion RPC anywhere in this file. Amending a policy means\n creating version N+1; that is what makes \"what did the policy say on the day\n Dennis acted\" answerable at all.\n\n DELIBERATELY ABSENT: any scope/binding field (\"who does this bind\"). §2 is\n explicit that the answer is a query over (person, context), not a field, and\n that the hierarchy which would feed it is unsettled. Inventing a scope field\n here would silently settle it. See the schematic looper's\n decisions/written-policy-scope-omitted.md (pre-split snoopy history, not in\n this repo).\n\n A stratum record since 2026-09-25, tenant-owned and not `private` — the block\n above `message Human` is the reasoning for all six and is not repeated.",
