            "description": "expires_at_ms is the lifetime. 0 MEANS PERMANENT, not \"expired at the\n epoch\" — the two lifetimes the filters doc names are \"time-expiring or\n permanent\", and a permanent rule has no expiry to state. An inferred filter\n is written with now + 24h per that doc's announced default; \"keep it\" is a\n correction that republishes the same node with 0 here.\n\n EXPIRY IS DATA, NOT AN EVENT. Nothing wakes at this timestamp and nothing\n rewrites the row when it passes — \"Expiry is silent\". The runtime compares\n it to now at evaluation time, and so does the app's read, which is also why\n it is RANGE-filterable.",
            "constraints": [
              "must be \u003e= 0"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_ge",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 0,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
