            "name": "supersedes",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "supersedes is the node_id this node replaced, if any — the chain a citation\n walks backwards. Empty on an original.\n\n It is what lets a text correction be a new node instead of an overwrite:\n the citation \"rule n-8f2c\" keeps resolving to the sentence that was\n actually in force, and the replacement says which one it grew out of.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 64 bytes"
