            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 64,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "deleted",
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "deleted is the soft-delete flag and the whole deletion mechanism. A deleted\n node is inert for evaluation, still visible in the history view, and still\n resolvable by a citation until it is purged.\n\n (spec.deleted_flag) — the 2026-09-20 stratum-record-lifecycle record's\n marker, which the pin now carries. It makes the generated query plane\n exclude these rows from List / Watch / Count / Sample by default, and it is\n what residency.deleted_max_age_seconds above measures the year from. Get by\n node_id still returns the row, deleted or not, until it is purged — which\n is the citation guarantee."
          },
          {
            "name": "created_ms",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "created_ms never moves again — not on a correction, not on a move, not on a\n delete. updated_ms is the business clock of the last write and is the\n retention timestamp_field. Both RANGE-filterable: \"what rules did I set\n last spring\" is the question a months-long history exists to answer.",
